{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nA ticket can carry so many acceptance criteria that one completion-verification run strains to\ncover them all, and nothing usefully warns the author. The motivating case was a 14-AC ticket\n(`9fd4`) that produced no size signal at all.\n\n**What already exists — established by direct inspection of `origin/main` on 2026-08-09. This\nchanges the ticket's shape substantially, and most of the originally-proposed work is already\nbuilt.**\n\n`p4_oversize` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py:371`) is a DET check that already fires on\nALL tickets (no leaf scoping), is already advisory and never blocks, and already carries THREE size\ndimensions:\n\n- `P4_AC_SOFT_CAP = 25` checklist items (`_count_ac_items`, :169 — counts `- [ ]` and `- [x]` under\n  an exact `## Acceptance Criteria` heading, via `evaluate_plan_clarity`)\n- `P4_FILE_IMPACT_SOFT_CAP = 30` file-impact entries\n- `P4_DESC_SOFT_CAP_CHARS = 24_000` description characters\n\nSo the description-length dimension **already exists** and does not need adding. All three signals\naccumulate into a single `signals` list inside ONE `DetResult`, so a long description and a high AC\ncount produce one finding with two evidence lines, never two competing findings — the\nduplicate-reporting this ticket set out to prevent is already impossible by construction. No\nsuppression mechanism is needed or wanted.\n\nAC-text quality is likewise already covered by three checks, not zero:\n\n- `p6_ac_quality` (`det_floor.py:470`, ADVISORY, never blocks) already detects **compound-AND\n  criteria** — \"one item bundling multiple deliverables joined by ' and '\" — via a lexical\n  heuristic (`\\band\\b` present AND commas+ands >= 2) and already emits the coaching \"split so each\n  is independently verifiable\". It also lints verify-commands, operator-attested evidence kinds,\n  measurement provenance, and cross-ticket citations.\n- `p11_ac_vagueness` (`det_clarity.py:182`, **BLOCKING**) applies a fixed vague/subjective lexicon\n  to AC item lines only.\n- `p6` additionally scans the WHOLE plan text with that same lexicon, advisory.\n\nBoth operate per-AC-line through the shared `det_operator_attested.ac_item_lines()` helper — the\nestablished seam for any further per-criterion check.\n\n**The two REAL gaps, after that inventory:**\n\n1. **The AC soft cap was never derived from data.** 25 is a hardcoded module constant, far above the\n   observed pain point — it would NOT have fired on the 14-AC ticket that motivated this work.\n2. **Nothing detects a VACUOUS acceptance criterion.** Searched `det_floor.py`, `det_clarity.py`,\n   every `plan_review/*.py`, `criteria_routing.json` and the reviewer prompts: no check flags a\n   criterion whose truth is already established by a gate that runs regardless — \"children are\n   complete\", \"tests pass\", \"CI is green\", \"lint/typecheck clean\". `p1` records literally BLANK\n   items and `F1` flags effort-framed/subjective ones, but a vacuous criterion is measurable, true,\n   and useless: it inflates the count while proving nothing the ticket is responsible for.\n\nGap 2 is what makes a raw count a poor proxy for \"should be split\". The same nominal count spans\nwildly different weights — a compound, detailed, genuinely load-bearing criterion counts the same as\n\"tests pass\". Calibrating the cap without removing vacuous items from the picture would just move\nan arbitrary number.\n\n## Inherited motivation (ticket 12b7, closed won't-fix 2026-08-09)\n\n`12b7` proposed sharding the completion verifier into parallel per-criterion runs because many-AC\nclosures strain a single completion-verification run. It was closed WON'T FIX: the sequential loop\nit targeted no longer exists, and per-criterion fan-out was already built, measured, and removed for\nexploding token/wall-clock cost. Its **cure** is dead; its **cause** is not. Preventing oversized AC\nsets is the surviving, prevention-side response to that pain, and it lands here. (The separate\nconcern — the monolithic PRIMARY completion call as wall-clock critical path — is not this ticket's\nand should be re-filed against the current batched architecture.)\n\n## Design constraint from ticket f391 — no grade-independent impact floor\n\n`f391` analysed the `undecomposed` axis and found the failure mode this ticket must not repeat: that\naxis forces a finding's impact to a fixed 0.85 REGARDLESS of the reviewer's severity grade, so a\n`low`-graded finding scores like a `high` one. In 25 of 29 fires it was the only hard override\npresent, and one ticket blocked at 0.6072 against a 0.60 line when its impact without the floor was\n0.0. Ticket-sizing is exactly the judgment-heavy signal where that goes wrong, so nothing here may\nacquire a grade-independent floor.\n\n## Plan\n\n**Part A — calibrate the caps from history instead of guessing.** Replay the persisted\n`*-REVIEW_RESULT.json` sidecar corpus under `.tickets-tracker/` (the zero-LLM-cost instrument `f391`\nestablished) together with the ticket store, and find where AC count actually starts predicting\ntrouble: tickets later split, reopened, or whose completion verification had to shard or recover.\nReport the distribution, not just a number. Do the same for the description-length cap while the\ninstrument is in hand. Make both caps config-driven rather than module constants.\n\nCount vacuous items separately when calibrating, so the cap is derived from LOAD-BEARING criteria\nrather than from padded counts.\n\nThe goal is right-sized tickets, NOT punishing thorough authors: prefer a cap that fires where\nsplitting genuinely helps, and accept false negatives over false positives on an advisory signal.\n\n**Part B — add vacuity detection to `p6_ac_quality`; do NOT add a new criterion.** Extend the\nexisting advisory DET check with a vacuous-criterion detector over `ac_item_lines()`, emitting\ncoaching to DROP the item because a gate already proves it. Extending `p6` keeps this deterministic,\nadvisory, and zero-LLM-cost, and reuses the per-AC-line seam the compound and vagueness checks\nalready share. Adding a routed LLM criterion for this would cost tokens on every review to\nre-discover something a lexicon settles.\n\n**Part C — assess, do not duplicate, the existing compound-AC detector.** `p6`'s compound check is a\nlexical `and`+comma heuristic. Measure its precision/recall against the same historical corpus and\nimprove it only if the measurement justifies it. Do not add a second compound-AC detector.\n\n**Part D — no suppression machinery.** Keep description length inside `p4_oversize`. P4 (\"this unit\nlooks big\") and P6 (\"these specific criteria are weak\") are different claims and may both fire; that\nis not duplication.\n\n## Testing\n\nPart A's calibration is an analysis: verification is that the distribution and chosen caps are\nreproducible from the stated corpus, with the denominator stated.\n\nPart B needs DET unit tests in the established `p6` pattern: fixtures for each vacuous shape\n(\"children complete\", \"tests pass\", \"CI green\", \"lint passes\"), and — critically — a NEGATIVE\ncontrol that is long, detailed and thorough but load-bearing, which must NOT be flagged. Without\nthat control the detector cannot be shown to avoid punishing thoroughness.\n\nRetuning the P4 caps must not change P4's posture: pin that it still never blocks and that its\nsignals still accumulate into one finding.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The AC-count soft cap is derived from a replay of historical tickets, with the distribution,\n      the chosen threshold, and the denominator recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] Vacuous criteria are excluded when deriving the cap, so it reflects load-bearing criteria.\n- [ ] The AC-count and description-length soft caps are config-driven rather than module constants,\n      defaulting to the derived values.\n- [ ] The description-length dimension remains inside `p4_oversize`; no separate description-length\n      check is added and no suppression mechanism is introduced.\n- [ ] `p4_oversize` still fires on ALL tickets and still never blocks, pinned by a test.\n- [ ] `p6_ac_quality` gains a vacuous-criterion detector that flags an AC already established by a\n      gate which runs regardless, and coaches dropping it.\n- [ ] The vacuity detector is advisory and cannot block a claim.\n- [ ] A negative-control fixture — long, detailed, thorough, load-bearing — is NOT flagged as\n      vacuous, demonstrating thoroughness is not penalized.\n- [ ] `p6`'s existing compound-AND detector is measured against the historical corpus and either\n      left as-is with that evidence recorded, or improved — but NOT duplicated by a second detector.\n- [ ] Nothing added here applies a grade-independent impact floor: a test asserts a lower-severity\n      finding yields a lower impact than a higher-severity one."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786328935111840001,"uuid":"cb2a17ba-fda5-4f21-bc46-6210329690fa"}